From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] elf64-ppc: refuse multiple TOC groups in a compact-.opd link

When the TOC reached by small-model TOC references (R_PPC64_TOC16,
-mcmodel=small or hand-written @toc) passes 64 KiB, ld splits the input
objects into several TOC groups and enters a function in another group
through a TOC-adjusting stub:

    std  r2,40(r1)          # stub
    addis r2,r2,adj ; addi r2,r2,adj ; b target
    ...
    ld   r2,40(r1)          # the nop after the bl, rewritten

The compact descriptors themselves come out right (each .opd's .TOC.
word resolves to its own object's group), but the hybrid ILP32 ABI keeps
the saved TOC in the WORD at 40(r1): GCC saves it with stw and restores
it with lwz after every indirect call, and often hoists the save into the
prologue.  The stub's std writes the zero high half of r2 over that word,
so the next lwz restore loads r2 = 0 and the following TOC access faults.
Measured on a two-group link (24 objects x 1000 TOC entries, ILP32,
-mcmodel=small): main saves r2 once with stw in its prologue, calls
f_16..f_23 through TOC-adjusting stubs, restores with lwz after its first
indirect call and gets r2 = 0; its next TOC load faults (RPCS3 PPU
interpreter: EA 0xffffffffffff80e4 = 0 - 0x7f1c).  The same objects in
one TOC group run clean.  LP64 code saves r2 with std/ld and
is not known to break, but it is refused too: Lv-2 links never needed
multiple TOC groups (the default medium code model reaches 2 GiB of TOC
from one base) and the multi-group path has no runtime coverage there.

Fix: when the multi-TOC layout decides more than one group is needed and
any input has a compact .opd (alignment below 8, the test patches 0002
and 0004 use), fail the link with a diagnostic naming the remedy.
ELFv1 links are unchanged.

--- a/bfd/elf64-ppc.c
+++ b/bfd/elf64-ppc.c
@@ -12879,6 +12879,35 @@
 
   htab->multi_toc_needed = htab->toc_curr != elf_gp (info->output_bfd);
 
+  /* Cell OS Lv-2: a link-time TOC-adjusting stub saves r2 with std and
+     the nop after the call becomes ld, but hybrid ILP32 code keeps its
+     saved TOC in the word at 40(r1) (stw/lwz around indirect calls,
+     often hoisted to the prologue).  The stub's std writes the zero high
+     word over it and the next lwz loads r2 = 0.  Refuse any link with a
+     compact .opd that would need more than one TOC group.  */
+  if (htab->multi_toc_needed)
+    for (ibfd = info->input_bfds; ibfd != NULL; ibfd = ibfd->link.next)
+      {
+	asection *opd;
+
+	if (!is_ppc64_elf (ibfd))
+	  continue;
+	opd = bfd_get_section_by_name (ibfd, ".opd");
+	if (opd != NULL
+	    && opd->size != 0
+	    && (opd->flags & SEC_EXCLUDE) == 0
+	    && OPD_COMPACT_P (opd))
+	  {
+	    info->callbacks->einfo
+	      (_("%X%P: error: Cell OS Lv-2 compact .opd link needs multiple "
+		 "TOC groups (over 64 KiB of TOC reached by small-model TOC "
+		 "references; first compact .opd in %pB), which is not "
+		 "supported; compile with -mcmodel=medium (the default) or "
+		 "-mminimal-toc\n"), ibfd);
+	    break;
+	  }
+      }
+
   if (!htab->do_multi_toc)
     return false;
 
